WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:04.930
I want to start this next segment with a reminder
or sort of a notice, I guess.

00:00:04.930 --> 00:00:08.610
And I don't know that people are necessarily
thinking in these terms.

00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:10.310
The election is about to get going.

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:11.740
Voting starts in six weeks.

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:16.690
The first absentee ballots are going to be
going out in North Carolina on September 4th.

00:00:16.690 --> 00:00:19.640
In Pennsylvania, they go out on September
14th.

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:20.640
In Michigan.

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:22.060
They go out on September 19th.

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:25.050
And this is incredibly important for a few
reasons.

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:29.779
Number one, Trump doesn't really have three
and a half months to to fix something or to

00:00:29.779 --> 00:00:32.390
have some big win to get voters back.

00:00:32.390 --> 00:00:34.590
For many voters, he has six weeks.

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:38.840
And when you look at those three states that
will most soon be voting.

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:44.670
Biden is up ahead, is up by two in North Carolina,
up by seven in Pennsylvania and up by seven

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:45.670
in Michigan.

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:49.350
Those are averages of recent pollings, according
to Real Clear Politics.

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:55.290
This means that the election is essentially
now Trump has six weeks to turn around the

00:00:55.290 --> 00:01:00.360
polls in those states because as people start
voting in September and October, that leaves

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:04.920
fewer people whose minds can be changed in
the second half of October.

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:07.329
And in the last days before the election.

00:01:07.329 --> 00:01:10.479
So the closing arguments of the campaign,
as it were.

00:01:10.479 --> 00:01:12.830
Need to start happening very, very soon.

00:01:12.830 --> 00:01:18.810
In 2016, 47 million people voted before Election
Day, either within person early voting or

00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:20.520
vote by mail absentee.

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:25.149
The assumption this year because of Corona
virus is that there will be dramatically more

00:01:25.149 --> 00:01:30.149
than 47 million people voting either early
or by mail, especially by mail.

00:01:30.149 --> 00:01:34.039
I sent in my absentee ballot request form
yesterday.

00:01:34.039 --> 00:01:36.259
So this means a few different things.

00:01:36.259 --> 00:01:41.850
Number one, the vigilance about voter suppression
has to be escalated dramatically now.

00:01:41.850 --> 00:01:47.880
I've made an effort since last election not
to do the thing where I start talking about

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:48.880
voter suppression.

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:51.369
October 5th, right of the year of the election.

00:01:51.369 --> 00:01:54.350
We've been talking about voter suppression
for years at this point.

00:01:54.350 --> 00:01:55.759
We've been covering the voter purges.

00:01:55.759 --> 00:01:57.869
We've been covering the opposition to vote
by mail.

00:01:57.869 --> 00:02:00.819
We've been talking about voting machines and
all of it.

00:02:00.819 --> 00:02:02.270
So it should already be up.

00:02:02.270 --> 00:02:04.390
But we need to even talk more about that.

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:06.779
And I'm going to talk more about that on Friday.

00:02:06.779 --> 00:02:12.810
We would expect that the president will become
even more erratic sooner than later.

00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:16.400
But really, we now need to realize what it
is that we're doing here.

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:21.500
You know, people talk about the most important
election of my life.

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:25.709
I believe this is the most important election
I will be voting in.

00:02:25.709 --> 00:02:30.040
So, you know, we talked a little bit about
this on the bonus show before.

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:31.390
Think about the 2012 election.

00:02:31.390 --> 00:02:34.060
Barack Obama had been president for four years.

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:39.569
Significant recovery from the Great Recession
of 2008.

00:02:39.569 --> 00:02:41.340
Economic expectations were positive.

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:48.780
And you can find clips of me saying in October
of 2012, I'm voting for Obama over Mitt Romney.

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:54.239
But the reality is that if Romney wins, we're
probably going to have a good economy for

00:02:54.239 --> 00:02:56.070
the for the next four years.

00:02:56.070 --> 00:03:03.200
All indicators were that the traditional economic
signals were pretty solid, that the economic

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:07.370
policy of Mitt Romney would certainly tweak
the trajectory a little bit.

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:10.269
But Romney had a different tax policy idea.

00:03:10.269 --> 00:03:12.640
Romney had a different health policy idea.

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:17.719
But generally speaking, whoever won in 2012
was going to preside over for relatively good

00:03:17.719 --> 00:03:21.409
years in the economy by all of the standard
measures.

00:03:21.409 --> 00:03:24.769
This is a very different situation than what
we have today.

00:03:24.769 --> 00:03:28.290
And so it wasn't that the 2012 election wasn't
important.

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:32.909
But even at the time, not just in retrospect,
I remember having the recognition and it's

00:03:32.909 --> 00:03:34.080
on record and video clips.

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:39.659
You can go, in fact, check me that this was
not the most important election I was participating

00:03:39.659 --> 00:03:40.659
in.

00:03:40.659 --> 00:03:44.890
We now we're in a situation where we will
either have four years of damage done by a

00:03:44.890 --> 00:03:53.019
reactionary, ignorant buffoon or we are going
to have eight years of an even more compromised,

00:03:53.019 --> 00:03:57.189
more unhinged Trump in the ladder, four of
those eight years.

00:03:57.189 --> 00:04:02.989
We are sort of on the precipice of either
diving even deeper into the deep end of ignorance

00:04:02.989 --> 00:04:07.819
and narcissism, or we can start to get the
house in order.

00:04:07.819 --> 00:04:11.230
We can start to regain respect from our traditional
allies.

00:04:11.230 --> 00:04:15.430
We can start to get away from being the laughing
stock that we have become.

00:04:15.430 --> 00:04:17.170
We can resume dealing with the climate crisis.

00:04:17.170 --> 00:04:19.650
We've gone the opposite direction on climate.

00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:25.830
And fortunately, Joe Biden has adopted elements
from the Green New Deal and from Bernie Sanders

00:04:25.830 --> 00:04:26.830
climate platform.

00:04:26.830 --> 00:04:27.889
So is it perfect?

00:04:27.889 --> 00:04:33.210
No, but we know, you know, this analogy or
this this example of if a boat leaves.

00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:36.650
New York across the Atlantic Ocean.

00:04:36.650 --> 00:04:41.639
What after 10 miles is only a difference of
a few hundred yards in terms of the angle

00:04:41.639 --> 00:04:46.790
can end up with you in Europe or Africa as
you cross the Atlantic Ocean.

00:04:46.790 --> 00:04:50.669
So that's the importance of starting to right
the ship today.

00:04:50.669 --> 00:04:56.250
We hopefully would be seeing an increase rather
than a decrease in the number of people with

00:04:56.250 --> 00:04:57.420
health insurance.

00:04:57.420 --> 00:05:02.680
If Joe Biden were to win in November, we could
stop worrying that if a Supreme Court justice

00:05:02.680 --> 00:05:07.910
were to get sick or die or retire, it would
plague us with decades more of the conservative

00:05:07.910 --> 00:05:09.610
nonsense that we've been seeing.

00:05:09.610 --> 00:05:11.600
So these are not trivial matters.

00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:13.889
And I know it feels like a way off.

00:05:13.889 --> 00:05:16.360
November is more than three months for some
voters.

00:05:16.360 --> 00:05:17.710
It starts in six weeks.

00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:22.330
For many voters, the decision about who they're
going to vote for is going to be made in the

00:05:22.330 --> 00:05:25.639
next four to five weeks and they will vote
in six weeks.

00:05:25.639 --> 00:05:28.509
So time is flying right now for a lot of us.

00:05:28.509 --> 00:05:30.699
The days look quite similar.

00:05:30.699 --> 00:05:35.789
Those of us who are still socially distancing
for months in quarantine each day felt long,

00:05:35.789 --> 00:05:38.520
but the four months have just flown by.

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:40.229
Six weeks are going to fly by.

00:05:40.229 --> 00:05:42.080
The next three months are going to fly by.

00:05:42.080 --> 00:05:48.080
And if I don't feel that I've done everything
I can to stop this insanity, I would not be

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:49.610
able to live with myself.

00:05:49.610 --> 00:05:51.639
So it is now election time.

00:05:51.639 --> 00:05:56.069
We've got the conventions coming up in whatever
form they take place.

00:05:56.069 --> 00:06:01.270
We have potentially debates coming up and
voting starts in six weeks.

00:06:01.270 --> 00:06:06.090
The opportunity will be there for October
surprises and then that's it.

00:06:06.090 --> 00:06:08.220
I mean, this thing is almost over.

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:12.949
Are we going to have four more years of utter
depravity or can we remove this lunacy from

00:06:12.949 --> 00:06:14.790
the Oval Office and start to.

00:06:14.790 --> 00:06:15.790
It's just the start.

00:06:15.790 --> 00:06:17.800
It's just turning the ship.

00:06:17.800 --> 00:06:24.569
Can we start to reintroduce sanity to our
federal leadership?

00:06:24.569 --> 00:06:28.250
And of course, one of the biggest issues to
consider is coronavirus.

00:06:28.250 --> 00:06:29.250
And that's what I want to talk about a little
bit.

00:06:29.250 --> 00:06:29.251
Next,

